# ── Two deliberate exclusions. Reasons recorded per §12. ──────────────────────

# Prose docs. Prettier's markdown printer reflows hand-tuned tables and lists —
# churn with no consistency win. §12's argument for Prettier is about
# agent-authored *code* drift, not prose.
*.md

# Markup. prettier-plugin-astro CHANGES RENDERED OUTPUT and cannot be made not
# to: it reformats inside Astro expressions, where htmlWhitespaceSensitivity
# does not reach, turning `<span class="dot">●</span>{t}` into
# `<span class="dot">\n●\n</span>\n{t}`. Whitespace around inline elements is
# significant in HTML, so that is a real change, not cosmetic — measured at 8/8
# pages altered on this repo. Formatting .ts/.css is provably output-neutral
# (verified: all pages and the emitted CSS byte-identical across the reformat),
# so the gate keeps its value for the files agents actually edit.
# Removal trigger: re-enable when the plugin honors whitespace sensitivity
# inside expressions, AND the reformat is verified to leave built HTML
# byte-identical. Do not re-enable on the strength of a green `astro check` —
# it does not compare output.
*.astro
